<div class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">BENCHMARKS / RELEASE HISTORY</p><h1>Generation time,<br>with the details.</h1><p class="intro">The same API shapes, measured across grape-oas releases. Compare versions within each table. Lower milliseconds are better.</p></div>
<div class="wrap benchmark-content">
<% if report %>
  <div class="report-summary"><div><span class="eyebrow">RUN AT</span><strong><%= h(report.fetch('generated_at')) %></strong></div><div><span class="eyebrow">RUBY / GRAPE</span><strong><%= h(report.fetch('environment').fetch('ruby').split.first(2).join(' ')) %> / <%= h(report.fetch('environment').fetch('dependencies').fetch('grape')) %></strong></div><div><span class="eyebrow">MEASUREMENT</span><strong><%= report.fetch('methodology').fetch('iterations') %> samples · JIT disabled</strong></div></div>
  <div class="report-actions"><a href="<%= url("benchmarks/runs/#{report_name}/results.json") %>">Download raw JSON ↗</a><a href="<%= url("benchmarks/runs/#{report_name}/RESULTS.md") %>">Markdown report ↗</a><a href="#methodology">Methodology ↓</a></div>
  <p class="reading-note">Negative changes mean faster generation; positive changes mean slower generation. These synthetic workloads measure route-count scaling, excluding API setup and JSON serialization. Small differences can reflect measurement noise.</p>
  <% report.fetch('methodology').fetch('routes').each do |routes| %>
  <section class="route-section"><p class="eyebrow">API SIZE</p><h2><%= routes.to_s.reverse.gsub(/(\d{3})(?=\d)/, '\1,').reverse %> routes</h2>
    <% BenchmarkReport::FORMAT_NAMES.each do |format, name| %>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="<%= routes %> routes, <%= name %>" tabindex="0"><table class="benchmark-table"><caption><%= name %></caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Version / commit</th><th scope="col">Median <span>ms</span></th><th scope="col">Range <span>ms</span></th><th scope="col">vs previous</th><th scope="col">vs oldest</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <% BenchmarkReport.rows(report, routes, format).each do |row| %>
      <tr class="<%= 'main-row' if row[:label] == 'main' %>"><th scope="row"><%= h(row[:label]) %><a class="commit-link" href="<%= repo("commit/#{row[:sha]}") %>"><%= row[:sha][0, 8] %></a></th><td><%= row[:error] ? 'Failed' : BenchmarkReport.number(row[:median]) %></td><td><%= BenchmarkReport.number(row[:min]) %>–<%= BenchmarkReport.number(row[:max]) %></td><td><%= BenchmarkReport.percent(row[:previous]) %></td><td><%= BenchmarkReport.percent(row[:baseline]) %></td></tr>
      <% if row[:error] %><tr><td colspan="5" class="failure"><%= h(row[:error]) %></td></tr><% end %>
    <% end %></tbody></table></div>
    <% end %>
  </section>
  <% end %>
  <section class="methodology" id="methodology"><p class="eyebrow">REPRODUCIBILITY</p><h2>What we measured</h2><p>One warmup generation per case, followed by <%= report.fetch('methodology').fetch('iterations') %> measured calls to <code>GrapeOAS.generate</code>. Timing uses Ruby’s monotonic clock. API construction and JSON serialization happen outside the timed operation. Garbage collection stays enabled.</p><p>Each version runs in a separate process with the same Ruby and locked dependencies. Format order is 2.0, 3.0, then 3.1. The API defines an integer path parameter and an optional string query parameter on each route. These results do not measure entity or contract introspection, HTTP throughput, or first-generation startup cost.</p><dl class="environment-list"><div><dt>Ruby</dt><dd><%= h(report.fetch('environment').fetch('ruby')) %></dd></div><div><dt>System</dt><dd><%= h(report.fetch('environment').fetch('os')) %></dd></div><div><dt>CPU</dt><dd><%= h(report.fetch('environment').fetch('cpu')) %></dd></div><div><dt>Harness</dt><dd><a href="<%= repo("commit/#{report.fetch('harness_sha')}") %>"><%= report.fetch('harness_sha')[0, 8] %></a><%= ' (working tree modified)' if report.fetch('harness_dirty') %></dd></div></dl><details><summary>Exact dependencies and environment</summary><%= code(JSON.pretty_generate(report.fetch('environment'))) %></details><p>Compare runs only when the environment, lockfile, and harness match. Rerun release baselines after changing any of them.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= repo('tree/website') %>">Runner and reproduction instructions ↗</a></section>
<% else %>
  <section class="methodology"><h2>No measurements published yet</h2><p>Reports appear here after a local benchmark run. Results are published with raw samples and environment details.</p><a href="<%= repo('tree/website') %>">Benchmark tooling ↗</a></section>
<% end %>
<section class="archive"><p class="eyebrow">PREVIOUS MEASUREMENTS</p><h2>Run archive</h2><ul><% reports.each do |name, archived| %><li><a href="<%= url("benchmarks/runs/#{name}/") %>"><%= h(archived.fetch('generated_at')) %><span><%= h(archived.fetch('environment').fetch('ruby').split.first(2).join(' ')) %> ↗</span></a></li><% end %></ul></section>
</div>
